    "name": "EZ Key Auth Attempts m2m",
    "description": "Collection for authentication attempt operations via the M2M (machine-to-machine) API.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe M2M API is dedicated to backend integrations that initiate MFA authentication on behalf of their users. It runs on a separate port (7080) and accepts **only API key authentication** (HTTP Basic Auth with `integrationKey:secretKey`). No admin bearer token paths exist in this API.\n\nThe integration identity is always derived from the API key credential — integrating applications never need to specify an `integrationId` in the request body.\n\n## Endpoints\n\n- **Create Auth Attempt**: Initiate a new MFA authentication request for a user\n- **Wait for Response**: Long-poll for device response with configurable timeout and polling interval\n- **Cancel Auth Attempt**: Abort a pending or read attempt (marks it EXPIRED)\n\n## Authentication\n\nAll endpoints require **HTTP Basic Auth** (API key):\n- Username: `integrationKey` (environment variable)\n- Password: `secretKey` (environment variable)\n\nBefore using this collection, create an API key via the Admin API (`EZ Key API Keys admin`) and set the `integrationKey` and `secretKey` environment variables.\n\n## Identification Strategies\n\nThe create endpoint supports two ways to identify the target enrollment:\n- **enrollmentId**: Direct reference — preferred for precision in multi-device scenarios\n- **userIdentifier**: Indirect lookup by username/user ID — convenient for single-device users\n\nAt least one must be provided. When both are given they are validated for consistency.\n\n## Rate Limiting\n\n- **Create**: 100 requests per minute per integration key\n- **Wait**: 200 requests per minute per integration key\n- Exceeded limits return HTTP 429 with a RFC 9457 problem detail response\n\n## Base URL\n\nUses `{{base_url_m2m_api}}` environment variable (default: `http://localhost:7080`).\n\n## Virtual Threads\n\nThe M2M API is configured with `spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true`. The wait endpoint performs a blocking long-poll that parks the virtual thread rather than occupying a platform thread, enabling high concurrency at low cost.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "4087"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "create",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"authAttemptId\", jsonData.authAttemptId);",
              "",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains authAttemptId\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('authAttemptId');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.authAttemptId).to.be.a('number');",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    pm.test(\"Response may contain authAttemptChallenge\", function () {",
              "        if (jsonData.hasOwnProperty('authAttemptChallenge') && jsonData.authAttemptChallenge !== null) {",
              "            pm.expect(jsonData.authAttemptChallenge).to.be.a('number');",
              "            pm.expect(jsonData.authAttemptChallenge).to.be.at.least(0);",
              "            pm.expect(jsonData.authAttemptChallenge).to.be.at.most(999999);",
              "        }",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains timeoutSeconds\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('timeoutSeconds');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.timeoutSeconds).to.be.a('number');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.timeoutSeconds).to.be.above(0);",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains expiresAt\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('expiresAt');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.expiresAt).to.be.a('string');",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    console.log('authAttemptId saved:', jsonData.authAttemptId);",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
