          "host": [
            "{{base_url_m2m_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "auth-attempts"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates a new authentication attempt for MFA validation via the M2M API.\n\n**Authentication:**\nHTTP Basic Auth with `integrationKey:secretKey`. The integration is always derived from the API key — do not include `integrationId` in the body.\n\n**Request Body:**\nProvide `enrollmentId` OR `userIdentifier` (at least one required):\n- `enrollmentId` (optional): Direct enrollment ID — must belong to the API key's integration\n- `userIdentifier` (optional): Username/user ID for enrollment lookup within the API key's integration. Returns 400 if multiple active enrollments are found for that user.\n- `challengeRequested` (required): Whether to generate a numeric challenge code displayed to the user\n\n**Response (201 Created):**\n- `authAttemptId`: Use this ID for subsequent `/wait` and `/cancel` calls\n- `authAttemptChallenge`: Numeric challenge to display to the user (null if not requested)\n- `timeoutSeconds`: Seconds until this attempt expires\n- `expiresAt`: Absolute expiration timestamp (ISO-8601 with timezone)\n\n**Challenge Flow:**\nWhen `challengeRequested: true`:\n1. Display the challenge code to the user\n2. User enters it on their mobile device\n3. User approves the authentication\n4. Call `/wait` to receive the result\n\n**Status Codes:**\n- 201: Auth attempt created successfully\n- 400: Validation error (missing fields, enrollment not found, enrollment not in ACTIVE status, multiple enrollments for userIdentifier)\n- 401: Invalid or missing API key\n- 403: Enrollment does not belong to this API key's integration\n- 429: Rate limit exceeded (100 requests per minute per integration key)\n- 500: Internal server error"
      },
      "response": []
    },
