        "description": "Creates an auth attempt using `userIdentifier` instead of `enrollmentId`. Use this variant when your application identifies users by username or user ID rather than by the internal ezkey enrollment ID.\n\n**When to use this variant:**\n- Your system stores a `userIdentifier` on the enrollment (set during provisioning)\n- The user has exactly one active enrollment in this integration\n\n**Multi-device constraint:**\nIf the user has multiple active enrollments (multiple devices), the API returns 400 with a message to specify `enrollmentId` instead.\n\n**Authentication:**\nHTTP Basic Auth with `integrationKey:secretKey`. Integration scope is automatic."
