        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_m2m_api}}/api/v1/auth-attempts/:id/wait?timeout=30&polling=2",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_m2m_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "auth-attempts",
            ":id",
            "wait"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "timeout",
              "value": "30",
              "description": "Maximum wait duration in seconds (1-300, default: 30)"
            },
            {
              "key": "polling",
              "value": "2",
              "description": "Polling interval in seconds (1-60, default: 2)"
            }
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "id",
              "value": "{{authAttemptId}}",
              "description": "Authentication attempt ID to wait on (saved from create response)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Long-polls for device response on a pending authentication attempt. The endpoint blocks (up to `timeout` seconds) and returns as soon as the device responds or the timeout is reached.\n\n**Authentication:**\nHTTP Basic Auth with `integrationKey:secretKey`. Access control ensures API keys can only wait on attempts belonging to their integration.\n\n**Path Parameters:**\n- `id` (required): The authentication attempt ID returned by the create endpoint\n\n**Query Parameters:**\n- `timeout` (optional, default 30): Maximum seconds to wait (1–300). The server-side long-poll duration.\n- `polling` (optional, default 2): Internal polling interval in seconds (1–60). Must be strictly less than `timeout`.\n\n**Virtual Thread behaviour:**\nThe blocking wait parks a virtual thread — no platform thread is held. This allows many concurrent wait calls at minimal resource cost.\n\n**Response (200 OK — device responded):**\n- `authAttempt`: Full auth attempt state (includes `authAttemptProofToken` when ACCEPTED)\n- `status`: Calculated status — `PENDING`, `READ`, `INVALID`, `REJECTED`, `ACCEPTED`, `EXPIRED`\n- `completed`: `true` when device has responded (ACCEPTED / REJECTED / INVALID)\n- `timeoutReached`: `false`\n- `waitDuration`: Actual seconds waited\n- `completedAt`: Timestamp of response\n\n**Response (408 Request Timeout — no response yet):**\nSame structure with `timeoutReached: true` and `completed: false`. Caller should retry.\n\n**Integration pattern:**\n```\nloop {\n  resp = GET /wait?timeout=30\n  if resp.completed → break\n  if resp.timeoutReached → continue  // retry\n}\n```\n\n**Status Codes:**\n- 200: Device responded (check `status` field)\n- 408: Timeout reached, attempt still pending\n- 400: Invalid parameters (timeout/polling out of range, polling >= timeout)\n- 401: Invalid or missing API key\n- 403: Attempt does not belong to this integration\n- 404: Auth attempt not found\n- 429: Rate limit exceeded (200 requests per minute per integration key)\n- 500: Internal server error"
      },
      "response": []
    },
