        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_m2m_api}}/api/v1/auth-attempts/:id/cancel",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_m2m_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "auth-attempts",
            ":id",
            "cancel"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "id",
              "value": "{{authAttemptId}}",
              "description": "Authentication attempt ID to cancel"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Cancels a pending or read authentication attempt by marking it as EXPIRED. Use this to proactively abort an authentication request — for example when the user abandons the flow in your application.\n\n**Authentication:**\nHTTP Basic Auth with `integrationKey:secretKey`. Access control ensures API keys can only cancel attempts belonging to their integration.\n\n**Path Parameters:**\n- `id` (required): The authentication attempt ID to cancel\n\n**Cancellable states:**\nOnly `PENDING` and `READ` attempts can be cancelled. Attempting to cancel an attempt in a final state (`ACCEPTED`, `REJECTED`, `INVALID`, `EXPIRED`) returns 400.\n\n**Response (200 OK):**\n- `authAttemptId`: The cancelled attempt ID\n- `enrollmentId`: Associated enrollment\n- `authAttemptStatus`: `EXPIRED` — always EXPIRED after successful cancellation\n- `createdAt`: When the attempt was originally created\n- `expiresAt`: When the attempt was set to expire\n\n**Status Codes:**\n- 200: Attempt cancelled successfully (status is now EXPIRED)\n- 400: Attempt is already in a final state (cannot be cancelled)\n- 401: Invalid or missing API key\n- 403: Attempt does not belong to this integration\n- 404: Auth attempt not found\n- 500: Internal server error"
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "error scenarios",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "create - missing required field",
          "event": [
